1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,505
The doubling penny loses to a million bucks for twenty-seven days straight.

2
00:00:04,405 --> 00:00:08,313
So pick. A million today, or one penny that doubles daily for thirty days?

3
00:00:08,563 --> 00:00:12,361
Everybody says penny. Okay— okay, but do you actually know when it wins?

4
00:00:12,611 --> 00:00:16,781
Day ten, you've got five dollars and twelve cents. Hit like if you're already sweating.

5
00:00:17,081 --> 00:00:21,339
Day twenty? About five grand. The million's still like a hundred ninety times bigger.

6
00:00:21,639 --> 00:00:23,815
Send this to the friend who'd bail right here.

7
00:00:24,715 --> 00:00:29,452
Day twenty-seven: six hundred seventy-one thousand. Three days left, and you're still losing.

8
00:00:29,752 --> 00:00:32,875
'Cause seven eighths of the money shows up in those last three days.

9
00:00:33,725 --> 00:00:36,001
Follow, this page always finishes the math.

10
00:00:36,451 --> 00:00:41,316
Day twenty-eight, one point three million. Day thirty? Five point three seven million.

11
00:00:41,616 --> 00:00:44,350
So be honest: day twenty, are you still holding the penny?

